                <pb facs="0999" n="879" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg879"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2377: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-10T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 10,
                                1922—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Your no. 8 of January 7, 11 a.m. See the Minister for Foreign Affairs, … talk
                    with him along the lines indicated in our instructions of December 24, 1921, 3
                    p.m., and lay before him the plan outlined in that telegram. Present the plan
                    merely as a suggestion, however, so as to avoid the possibility that he will
                    immediately unconditionally reject it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
